            <head>Illustrations of the Family of Psittacidæ, or Parrots / The greater part of them species hitherto unfigured, containing forty-two lithographic plates, drawings from life, and on stone</head>
            <lg>
               <l>ILLUSTRATIONS</l>
               <l/>
               <l>of</l>
               <l/>
               <l>THE FAMILY OF PSITTACIDÆ,</l>
               <l>or</l>
               <l/>
               <l>PARROTS:</l>
            </lg>
            <lg>
               <l>THE GREATER PART OF THEM</l>
               <l/>
               <l>SPECIES HITHERTO UNFIGURED,</l>
               <l/>
               <l>CONTAINING</l>
               <l/>
               <l>FORTY-TWO LITHOGRAPHIC PLATES,</l>
               <l/>
               <l>DRAWINGS FROM LIFE, AND ON STONE,</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">By EDWARD LEAR, A.L.S.</p>
            <lg>
               <l>LONDON:</l>
               <l>PUBLISHED BY E. LEAR, 61 ALBANY STREET, REGENT'S PARK.</l>
               <l>1832.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">TO THE</p>
            <p rend="justify">Queen's Most Excellent Majesty,</p>
